Satellite Photometry Sources

Mike McCants / QuickSat
----------------------
Author: Mike McCants
Data: qs.mag, from qsmag.zip (file date 2020-09-14)
Source: https://www.mmccants.org/programs/qsmag.zip
Original software documentation: QUICKSAT.txt, preserved with this data.
Documentation source: https://mmccants.org/programs/quicksat.zip

The author's original distribution statement reads:
"This program is freeware. There are no restrictions on its distribution."

QUICKSAT.txt describes the magnitude as the maximum apparent brightness at
1000 km and full phase. The original source statements and attribution
accompany these materials; ASTROCHRON's Apache-2.0 license covers its own code.

Chinese Space Station Reference
-------------------------------
Observer: Jay Respler
Report date: 2022-08-03
Source: https://www.satobs.org/seesat/Aug-2022/0030.html
Reference value: 0.87 mag, QuickSat intrinsic-magnitude convention,
average of three observations. The report concerns the 2022 configuration;
module and spacecraft changes can alter its brightness.
